==Old Norse==

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|stainaz|lang=non}}, whence also Old English {{term|stan|stān|lang=ang}} (English {{term|stone}}, Scots {{term|stane|lang=sco}}), Old Frisian {{term|sten|stēn|lang=ofs}}, Old High German {{term|stein|lang=goh}} (German {{term|Stein|lang=de}}), Gothic {{term|𐍃𐍄𐌰𐌹𐌽𐍃|tr=stains|sc=Goth}}.

===Noun===
{{head|non|noun|g=m}}

# [[stone]]

